ee from that 2019 team. Despite all that, they were considered a team to watch. The Netherlands already had to be rated as strong favourites, having been the silver medallists at the 2019 World Championships, and more recently, European Champions in 2020 and 2021. Ireland was also considered a medal threat, having come third at the 2020 European Championships, and capturing second at the recent World Rowing Cup III."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The favourites all made it through to the finals, with Great Britain, China, and Poland rounding out the field. The Netherlands and Australia started out fastest and were neck and neck through the first 500m. Australia then began to separate themselves from the rest of the field, with the Dutch in closest pursuit. The Netherlands challenged one more time, but Australia held them off for the gold. Ireland took the bronze, edging out Great Britain and China."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "Australia"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUS.png"}] "AUS"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "8"} [:a {:href "/athletes/129044"} "Lucy Stephan"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/140650"} "Rosemary Popa"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/129043"} "Jess Morrison"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/140642"} "Annabelle McIntyre"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "Netherlands"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NED"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NED.png"}] "NED"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "8"} [:a {:href "/